  "faqAppBarTitulo": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
  "faqTooltipInicio": "Home",
  "faqBuscaHint": "Search questions and answers...",
  "faqNenhumaEncontrada": "No questions found.",
  "faqPergunta1": "Are emergency alerts sent to the registered numbers even if my phone is turned off or has no internet signal?",
  "faqResposta1": "Yes, the alarms on the \"Alarm\" page and the countdown timer on the \"Security\" page are scheduled on the Guardian-X app's database server. If the timer runs out of tolerance time without being disarmed with the PIN password, or the \"Alarm\" page alarm isn't disarmed after the tolerance time, a security alert with the last location recorded in the cloud is sent immediately.",
  "faqPergunta2": "How many minutes before the timer ends does the app start sending location to the Guardian-X database?",
  "faqResposta2": "Location starts being sent 120 minutes before the end of the timer or the scheduled time of the alarm on the Alarm page.",
  "faqPergunta3": "Why is a scheduled waiting period required to confirm a new password or to delete emergency contacts?",
  "faqResposta3": "Since the Guardian-X app aims to protect the user's safety, this waiting period exists to prevent unauthorized people from unlocking certain scheduled functions while the emergency alert is waiting to be sent to the registered numbers.",
  "faqPergunta4": "Why does the \"History\" page require the access PIN to view information about sent alert messages?",
  "faqResposta4": "In extreme cases where the user's physical safety is at risk, the user may decide that no one else should know their location or photo has been sent to a registered number — so viewing it requires confirming the user's own registered access PIN.",
  "faqPergunta5": "Why are two alert messages sent when the physical panic button or the \"Security\" page panic button is used?",
  "faqResposta5": "This panic button function has the user's safety as its top priority. When the physical panic button or the one on the \"Security\" page is triggered, an emergency alert message containing the location is sent immediately to the registered numbers. Then, after the device's camera opens and the user takes a photo, a second emergency alert message containing the photo is sent. This guarantees the location will reach the registered number even if the user takes time or doesn't take the photo.",
  "faqPergunta6": "Is it possible to track and follow the location of a device that doesn't have the Guardian-X app installed?",
  "faqResposta6": "No, it isn't possible. Location can only be shared from app to app, and only with the consent and permission of both users.",
  "faqPergunta7": "Is it safe to pay for the Premium plan?",
  "faqResposta7": "Yes, it's safe. No payment is made directly to the RMF GLOBAL company. All payments are processed directly through the Google Play Store or Apple App Store platform, with the platforms' full guarantee.",
  "faqPergunta9": "How are emergency alerts shared?",
  "faqResposta9": "All security alert messages are sent in two standard ways: from app to app, and by SMS to the mobile numbers registered on the \"Settings\" page.",
  "faqPergunta11": "How does the customer support service work?",
  "faqResposta11": "Customer support is now provided through an integrated Support Chat, right in the app and on the website — tap the support button on the Home screen to start a conversation. Your questions about the app, plans, and how to use it are answered instantly by an AI assistant. If the assistant can't safely resolve your issue, or if you'd rather talk to a person, just ask — the conversation is forwarded to a human agent on our team.",
  "faqPergunta12": "Will emergency alert messages only be sent to registered numbers that have the Guardian-X app installed?",
  "faqResposta12": "No. We recommend that both phones have the app installed, but even if the recipient's phone doesn't have Guardian-X, the emergency alert is still sent via SMS.",
  "faqPergunta13": "How can I use the panic buttons and how do they work?",
  "faqResposta13": "The panic buttons can be used by pressing the specific button on the Security page or by pressing and holding the volume-up button for 3 seconds. On some Android phone models, the camera opens automatically, making it possible to take the photo, while on other models it requires a confirmation from the native system to use the camera.",
  "termosAppBarTitulo": "Terms and Privacy",
  "termosTabContrato": "Consent Agreement",
  "termosTabPrivacidade": "Privacy Policy",
  "termosAvisoRodape": "This document summarizes the Guardian-X app's Consent Agreement and Privacy Policy. If you have questions, contact us through the support channels shown in the app.",
  "termosContratoTitulo1": "1. Purpose and Service Limits",
  "termosContratoCorpo1": "This Consent Agreement governs the use of the Guardian-X app, developed and operated by RMF Global LTDA (\"RMF Global\"), intended to assist the user in personal emergency situations through security check-ins, automatic alerts, location sharing between family members and trusted contacts, and photographic evidence capture. Guardian-X is a personal-safety aid tool and does NOT replace official emergency services (Military Police - 190, Fire Department - 193, SAMU - 192, or the equivalent emergency numbers in your country) or any other public emergency service. In an immediate risk situation, the user must always contact official emergency numbers first.",
  "termosContratoTitulo2": "2. Consent for location use (GPS and Background Location)",
  "termosContratoCorpo2": "By activating the check-in timer, the SOS button, or family monitoring, the user expressly consents to the collection and transmission of their real-time geographic location (GPS), including in the background (Background Location) when the app isn't actively in use, strictly to enable sending and saving preventive and panic alerts to Guardian-X's servers and to the registered emergency contacts, including automatically if the check-in isn't confirmed within the configured time.",
  "termosContratoTitulo3": "3. Consent for sending messages (SMS/App)",
  "termosContratoCorpo3": "The user consents to sending alert messages (containing location, informed context, and, when applicable, a photo) to the phone numbers and accounts registered as emergency contacts, via SMS and app-to-app notification.",
  "termosContratoTitulo4": "4. Consent for camera use and media capture",
  "termosContratoCorpo4": "The user consents that, in certain emergency scenarios (timer ending without confirmation, panic button activation, or a failed disarm attempt), the app may automatically open the device's camera to capture a photo, to be sent as additional evidence to the registered emergency contacts and saved to the Guardian-X database.",
  "termosContratoTitulo5": "5. Security waiting periods",
  "termosContratoCorpo5": "Certain sensitive actions (changing the password/PIN, deleting emergency contacts) are subject to a waiting period before taking effect, to prevent unauthorized third parties from disabling the user's security functions under duress. Viewing the sent alert history is protected by confirming the user's registered access PIN.",
  "termosContratoTitulo6": "6. Plans, pricing and payments",
  "termosContratoCorpo6": "The Free Plan unlocks all Premium features for up to 10 (ten) days each month, with the remaining days subject to the free plan's limits. The Premium Plan costs the amount shown in the app at the time of subscription, charged monthly, with unlimited access to all app features. Premium Plan subscriptions are processed exclusively through the Google Play Store and Apple App Store platforms, subject to those platforms' respective billing, refund, and consumer protection policies — RMF Global does not receive or process payments directly.",
  "termosContratoTitulo7": "7. Cancellation and refund",
  "termosContratoCorpo7": "Cancellation of the Premium Plan and any refunds strictly follow the official policies of the Google Play Store or Apple App Store, depending on the platform used for the subscription — RMF Global does not process cancellations or refunds directly.",
  "termosContratoTitulo8": "8. Customer Support (SAC)",
  "termosContratoCorpo8": "Customer support is provided via WhatsApp — the contact button on the Home screen opens a direct chat with our support team. Requests for human support follow the policy rules set by RMF Global, with Premium Plan users getting exclusive access to this human support within up to 48 (forty-eight) hours.",
  "termosContratoTitulo9": "9. Free, unambiguous consent and revocation",
  "termosContratoCorpo9": "By using the Guardian-X app and activating its security features, the user declares they freely, knowingly, and unambiguously consent to the collection and use of GPS, personal data, and media (photos) in emergency situations, as described in this Agreement. The user may revoke this consent at any time by uninstalling the app or requesting the deletion of their account and associated data through the support channels shown in the app, subject to the security waiting periods described in Section 5.",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo1": "1. Data collected and purpose",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo1": "To enable Guardian-X's security features, we collect: (a) real-time and background geographic location (GPS/Background Location), strictly for sending and saving preventive and panic alerts; (b) photos and other media automatically captured when the panic button or the Capture and Deterrence feature is triggered; (c) the user's registration data and the emergency contacts they provide (name and phone number); and (d) technical device data needed for alerts to work (connectivity status, app version).",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo2": "2. Purpose of data use",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo2": "The data collected is used exclusively to enable the app's security features: triggering emergency alerts, consented location sharing between users, sending photographic evidence, and maintaining the security event history of the user's own account.",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo3": "3. Storage and cloud",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo3": "Part of the data is stored locally on the device (encrypted local database), and part is synced with cloud services (Firebase/Firestore and media storage) operated by RMF Global, to ensure emergency alerts are delivered even if the user's device is turned off, destroyed, or loses connection after triggering.",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo4": "4. Sharing with third parties",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo4": "Location and photographic evidence are only shared with the emergency contacts expressly registered by the user, and — in the case of family monitoring — only with the explicit consent of both parties. We do not sell or share personal data with third parties for advertising purposes.",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo5": "5. Data security",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo5": "Passwords and PINs are stored encrypted. Access to sensitive functions (password changes, contact deletion) is protected by waiting periods, and the sent alert history is protected by PIN confirmation, as described in the Consent Agreement.",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo6": "6. User rights (data protection)",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo6": "Under applicable data protection law (such as Brazil's LGPD - Law No. 13.709/2018), the user may, at any time, request access to their personal data, correction of incorrect registration data, deletion of their account and stored personal data, and revocation of authorizations granted to monitoring contacts, through the support channels shown in the app.",
  "termosPrivacidadeTitulo7": "7. Contact",
  "termosPrivacidadeCorpo7": "Questions about this Privacy Policy can be sent to RMF Global LTDA (CNPJ 68.358.210/0001-90) through the support channels shown on the app's Home screen (WhatsApp and institutional address).",
